# secret-scan allowlist for THIS repo.
# One Python regex per line; a match on an added line suppresses a finding.
# Comments must be on their own line — an inline `#` becomes part of the regex.
#
# NOTE: this file is scanned like any other. Write each rule so its own text
# does not look like a secret — break the `keyword: value` shape with `\s`,
# a character class, or by matching the value alone.

# Skills document agent config directories, so allow a home root prefix
# (still catches real secrets/tokens/keys).
^.*/(Users|home)/[^/]+/(work|\.claude|\.agents|\.codex)/

# --- vendored NVIDIA device skills (Apache-2.0), skills/jetson-orin-nano/ ---
# Upstream files. The venv path is a generic Ubuntu default; the rest are
# variables that merely carry "token"/"password" in their NAME.
ubuntu/\.venvs/
^\s*token\s=\s_token\(
^\s*token[=](encode|decode)_token,$
^\s*password\s=\sparsed\.password$
must be a version token

# --- the scanner's own documentation describes what it detects ---
//user:password@host

# --- skill examples and test fixtures, never a real credential ---
# Dart: forwarding a parameter of the same name.
:\spassword\)
# Widget-test literal.
pw12345678
# Test-container default.
:\s"postgres",$
# Placeholder the user substitutes on the board.
<board-password>

# --- container test harness, test/ ---
# The image's own user directory. A container path, identical for everyone who
# runs the checks, so it identifies nobody.
/home/agent/
